# Lane: selftest — fixture for the hermetic-boundary regression spec.
#
# Not a CI matrix row and not an application test. Its `tasks` file runs
# no Ruby, no Node, and no application code: it reports the environment
# the boundary actually delivered so that
# spec/unit/lanes/hermetic_boundary_spec.rb can assert on it. The scrub
# block in tests/lanes/run is subtle enough that its last regression (an
# awk filter that matched only the `-fx` function attribute and so let
# `-ftx` functions through) was caught by human review rather than by a
# test; this lane is what makes the next one fail loudly instead.
#
# The three service URLs are blanked on purpose. tests/lanes/run builds
# REQUIRED_PORTS by matching 127.0.0.1:<port> in exactly these three
# values, so emptying them leaves the array empty — preflight passes,
# autostart never fires, and the lane finishes in milliseconds with no
# containers running. If the preflight ever learns to read a fourth
# endpoint, blank it here too or this lane starts requiring services.
AUTHENTICATION_MODE=simple
REDIS_URL=''
RABBITMQ_URL=''
AUTH_DATABASE_URL=''
